WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.843 --> 00:00:05.706
Dr. Tarun Mittal is a
surgeon in New Delhi.

00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:08.880
He's fighting on the front lines
of an epidemic quietly

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.480
sweeping India, driven
by a new menace:

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.481
junk food.

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:18.153
We reduce the size of the stomach,
which is called a sleeve gastrectomy.

00:00:18.153 --> 00:00:22.920
We have operated from
age of 13 till the age of 74.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.080
Initially, when I joined my practice,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.520
I was seeing maybe one
or two patients a month.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.000
Now I am seeing
15 to 20 patients a month.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.720
In India, almost one in four adults
is considered overweight or obese.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.040
If nothing changes, the country’s 
obesity rate

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.400
is set to increase by more
than 80% by 2035.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.400
This is not simply a story of individuals
making unhealthy lifestyle choices.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.920
In India, and much of the
world, larger economic

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.560
and social forces are threatening
people's health and prosperity.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:04.272
Much of India's history has been blighted by famine.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:09.480
As recently as 1943, the Bengal famine
killed up to three million people.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.760
Even now, roughly a third of children
suffer from stunted growth.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.600
And yet, over the last three
decades, obesity has surged.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.626
And it's set to get worse.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:21.331
That’s been accompanied by a rise

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.584
in cardiovascular disease and diabetes.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.337
The economic costs are enormous.

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:29.600
Premature deaths, health care costs

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.040
and productivity losses

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:31.049
Premature deaths, health care costs
and productivity losses

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.093
resulting from an overweight population

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.840
are estimated to top 

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.360
$129 billion by 2035,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:38.389
are estimated to top 

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:41.601
almost 2% of its GDP.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.270
It's a double burden
of malnutrition now.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.356
Malnutrition means under and over.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.442
Now we are seeing a lot of
overnutrition as well.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:53.029
Dr. Arun Gupta is a pediatrician
and health campaigner.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:55.740
He is the co-author
of The Junk Push, 

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.994
a report detailing how changing food consumption threatens health.

00:01:59.994 --> 00:02:05.291
Since globalization, the marketing of processed and ultra-processed food

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.376
has picked up.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:10.505
That has actually influenced
a lot of dietary habits.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:14.843
One of the major inputs
here is unhealthy diet comprising of ultra

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:19.180
ultra-processed foods, high in sugar, high in saturated fat,

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.766
or high in salt or sodium.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.061
Throughout the country,

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:29.232
home-cooked meals are losing out
to empty calories and sugar.

00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:30.441
In the span of a decade,

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:33.611
India's consumption of 
breakfast cereals and potato chips

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:35.029
have more than tripled,

00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:38.658
while confectionary items
and soda sales have doubled.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.036
India is a massive emerging market
for Western brands.

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:45.290
Sales of ultra-processed snack food
and sugary beverages

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:52.297
grew from $6.2 billion in 2009
to $32 billion in 2022.

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:55.967
For companies like Nestlé, Unilever
or Kellanova,

00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:59.179
sales are growing at double-digit rates.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.639
And who one are of the main targets?

00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:03.766
Whenever we go to a party,

00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:08.104
suppose a birthday party of
one friend, there'll be various

00:03:08.104 --> 00:03:11.733
junk food items such as Coke, Pepsi.

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.860
I really enjoy Maggi,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.070
and I like noodles and ramen.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:17.071
Burger King, McDonald's.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:17.697
Maggi.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.448
Pasta.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:18.907
Chips.

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:19.532
Burgers.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.158
Pizza.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.118
That is very delicious.

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:26.539
India's new food economy has created
a public health conundrum,

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:30.168
with the packaged food
and beverages industry increasingly

00:03:30.168 --> 00:03:34.005
affecting the diets of 1.4 billion Indians.

00:03:34.005 --> 00:03:38.009
One remedy that other countries have turned to is stricter regulation.

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:40.553
Chile, for example,
has an advertising ban

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.931
on television on certain foods

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:45.350
between 6 a.m. and 10 p.m.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.853
It also has restricted
the use of child-targeted imagery

00:03:48.853 --> 00:03:50.396
in the marketing of these products.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.316
After these interventions were introduced,

00:03:53.316 --> 00:03:56.069
sugary drink sales dropped by 24%,

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.154
as well as calorie consumption,

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:01.532
calories from sugar,
and calories from saturated fat.

00:04:02.158 --> 00:04:07.121
Until now, India has mostly relied on the companies themselves self-regulating

00:04:07.121 --> 00:04:10.750
how they convey the nutritional
value of their products.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.753
The results, some argue, are misleading.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:17.173
If you you see the front of the pack,
you will see that they claim that

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:20.385
it's like 50% of vitamin D.

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:23.263
Rich in vitamin C, no added preservatives.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.724
And it says very brightly, 20% protein.

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:32.063
But if you look at the back of the label,
you find that 46% of it is sugar.

00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:33.815
More than 13 grams of sugar.

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:37.694
Stabilizers, colors and flavors.

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:40.488
If you are telling people
that it is high in protein,

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:44.367
you very well tell them it is
high in sugar and high in fat, also.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:48.162
Efforts are underway to introduce
a more rigorous system.

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:50.248
Throughout 2021 and 2022,

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:53.918
Indian authorities consulted
health and consumer rights experts,

00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:58.381
and representatives of food companies,
about a new labeling system.

00:04:58.381 --> 00:05:02.260
While health and consumer rights groups argued for a traffic light system,

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.636
used by much of Europe,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.305
which signals red for products

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:07.265
high in sugar, fat or salt,

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:11.436
the eventual conclusion by the authority
was for a Health Star Rating,

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:15.857
which assigns star ratings for a product's
overall nutritional value.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.984
Not everyone was happy.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.279
Health Stars only point that this food is

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:24.657
either healthy or less healthy.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:27.327
It doesn't tell people
that it is unhealthy.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:31.497
For example, a pack of cookies
may have a very high amount of sugar.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.959
But, if the manufacturers add nuts,
it could get awarded a star

00:05:34.959 --> 00:05:36.836
for containing fiber.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.672
Getting that regulation right

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.091
has been evading us in the country.

00:05:42.091 --> 00:05:44.135
So that is one part of the story.

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:46.721
But what we are missing out is

00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:50.058
working at community level,

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:53.811
with children, with parents, families

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:56.481
to create an environment
for healthy eating

00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:59.067
and sustainable food environments.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:02.528
Pawan Agarwal runs
the Food Future Foundation,

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:06.741
a nonprofit that seeks to educate
schoolchildren about healthy eating.

00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:09.869
The foundation
runs programs in schools like this one

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.538
in order to educate children and parents.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:17.835
It is so important to focus
on preventive strategy

00:06:17.835 --> 00:06:24.342
and use diet and lifestyle
as the entry point for this intervention.

00:06:24.342 --> 00:06:29.639
Government or any regulatory body
cannot reach out to individual citizens

00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:31.099
at all mealtimes.

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:34.435
So at the end of the day,
this is about individual choices.

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:37.438
While nutrition advocates
seek tighter regulation,

00:06:37.438 --> 00:06:40.441
that may run at odds with
Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s

00:06:40.441 --> 00:06:44.695
strategy to attract more investment
from multinational companies.

00:06:44.695 --> 00:06:47.615
The fear among health experts
is that the burden will ultimately fall

00:06:47.615 --> 00:06:51.411
upon people to make
healthy choices on their own,

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:53.663
with little guidance from the government.

00:06:53.663 --> 00:06:58.584
One of the tactics they use is 
putting the onus on the people.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:02.380
That it is the people
who are choosing to eat wrong foods.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.423
It's not us.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.676
Which, probably is one of the strategies

00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:09.554
which they have been
using for tobacco, also.

00:07:09.554 --> 00:07:13.891
That people are smoking by
their choice and not because

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:14.892
of the marketing.

00:07:14.892 --> 00:07:16.436
What cigarette do you smoke, doctor?

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.271
The brand named most was Camel.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.149
Smoke Camels. The cigarette so
many doctors enjoy.

00:07:21.149 --> 00:07:25.778
The tactic is: industry will become
a part of the solution.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.864
They want to be a part of the solution.

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:31.242
They enter into policymaking bodies.

00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:33.161
Of course, the government

00:07:33.161 --> 00:07:34.704
allows them to do so,

00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:36.205
as stakeholders.

00:07:36.205 --> 00:07:38.291
Strict regulations and education

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:41.627
have driven down
smoking rates across the globe.

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:45.214
Imposing controls on the food
industry may be necessary

00:07:45.214 --> 00:07:49.927
to fight India's surging obesity rates
and the illnesses that it causes.

00:07:49.927 --> 00:07:55.600
Diabetes, hypertension, joint pains, back pain, varicose veins, gallbladder stone,

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.897
hernia, cancers, infertility,
chest problems, heart problems.

00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:03.733
It is putting an enormous
strain on our economy.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.112
A country once
blighted by too few calories,

00:08:08.112 --> 00:08:12.116
must face a new battle
with too many empty ones.

